cadence projects search: --limit takes an integer, not "many"

usage: cadence projects search --project PROJECT [--q Q] [--limit N]

Search entities of this project and the registry with free text and qualifiers (GET /projects/{p}:search, operation projects.search)

Search what Cadence knows — projects, mixes, registry versions and collections, jobs, approvals,
help articles — from this project. q is free text (typos and identifiers match by trigram; Hebrew
is matched without niqqud) plus qualifiers: kind:<kind>[,<kind>] (e.g. kind:dataset_version,job),
status:<s> (alias state:), lang:<locale> (he matches he-IL), actor:agent|user|automation|<id>,
updated:>2026-09-01 (also <, >=, <=, a day, or a..b), project:<slug> or scope:all|project|registry,
tag:<tag>, alias:@<name>, and numeric comparisons such as wer<10, progress>=0.5 or dur:2..8. Without
a scope qualifier the search covers this project and the registry. Results are grouped by kind, this
project's newest first. An unknown qualifier answers invalid-query with the list of qualifiers.

Flags:
  --project            Project slug [required]
  --q                  Free text plus qualifiers, e.g. `fleurs kind:dataset_version tag:telephony updated:>2026-09-01`
  --limit              Most hits returned over all groups [integer; default 50]

Global flags:
  --url URL               control plane (env CADENCE_URL, default http://127.0.0.1:8080; /api is appended)
  --token TOKEN           API key, sent as a Bearer token (env CADENCE_TOKEN; create one with credentials new)
  --idempotency-key KEY   commands only: reuse a key to replay a command's first result (default: a new key)
  -h, --help              this command's flags
